And once we were in that area of Barney's kind of attitude towards marriage, just being prejudiced against marriage and not to people, we somehow that led us to wait a second.
一旦我们处于巴尼对婚姻的态度的那种领域，只是对婚姻而不是对人有偏见，我们不知何故让我们等待了一秒钟。

00:51:42.989 --> 00:51:44.869
We don't know a lot about his upbringing.
我们对他的成长经历了解不多。

00:51:44.869 --> 00:51:48.150
We know he did not know his dad, we knew that.
我们知道他不认识他的父亲，我们知道这一点。

00:51:48.150 --> 00:51:51.630
We knew a little bit about Staten Island, a little bit about his mom.
我们对史泰登岛有一点了解，对他的妈妈也有一点了解。

00:51:51.630 --> 00:51:59.070
And we thought, what could be a surprising, fun way to really show that Barney had this very unique family situation?
我们想，怎样才能以一种令人惊讶、有趣的方式来真正展示巴尼拥有这种非常独特的家庭状况呢？

00:51:59.070 --> 00:52:00.550
And we wanted to give him somebody.
我们想给他一个人。

00:52:00.550 --> 00:52:05.269
We wanted to give him somebody else that he loved, somebody else that he looked up to.
我们想给他一个他爱的人，一个他尊敬的人。

00:52:05.269 --> 00:52:09.070
And we thought, it would be really interesting if Barney Stenson's brother is gay.
我们想，如果巴尼·斯滕森的兄弟是同性恋，那会很有趣。

00:52:09.070 --> 00:52:17.389
And then the idea that two of the two different dads, and I think down the line, we thought it would just be interesting that they each wanna find their dad and we'll probably do something without somebody.
然后，两个不同的父亲中的两个，我认为，我们认为这很有趣，他们每个人都想找到他们的父亲，我们可能会在没有人的情况下做一些事情。

00:52:17.389 --> 00:52:30.510
Right, could you imagine if Barney had also horrible politics in addition to everything else and be like, we can't have this guy be a serious regular, like you would be unbearable.
是的，你能想象如果巴尼除了其他一切之外还有可怕的政治吗，我们不能让这个人成为一个严肃的常客，就像你难以忍受一样。

00:52:30.510 --> 00:52:31.510
Yeah.
是的。

00:52:31.510 --> 00:52:36.510
This episode was nominated for a GLAD Media Award, Craig, do you recall this?
这一集获得了 GLAD 媒体奖提名，克雷格，你还记得吗？

00:52:36.510 --> 00:52:37.510
Oh, I forgot.
哦，我忘了。

00:52:37.510 --> 00:52:38.510
I forgot about that.
我忘了那件事了。

00:52:38.510 --> 00:52:39.510
That is an honor.
这是一种荣幸。

00:52:39.510 --> 00:52:40.510
I forgot about that.
我忘了那件事了。

00:52:40.510 --> 00:52:41.510
That's lovely.
太可爱了。

00:52:41.510 --> 00:52:53.570
Well, I think in some ways we talked about this a little bit, but contextualizing it in in a time where there was this like very kind of anti-gay marriage, Republican administration was in power.
嗯，我认为在某些方面我们对此进行了一些讨论，但是将其置于一个非常反同性婚姻的时代，共和党政府掌权的时代。

00:52:53.570 --> 00:53:05.389
And it, you know, even Obama, I was listening to, who was I listening to, someone as recline, but they were talking about, oh, oh, it taught us how he quotes the conversation he had with him.
你知道，即使是奥巴马，我也在听，我在听谁，有人斜倚，但他们在谈论，哦，哦，这教会了我们他如何引用他与他的谈话。

00:53:05.389 --> 00:53:06.389
I heard that too.
我也听说过。

00:53:06.389 --> 00:53:07.389
Yeah.
是的。

00:53:07.389 --> 00:53:10.989
You kind of forget that Obama at first was not, you know, all in on that.
你有点忘记了，你知道，奥巴马一开始并没有全力支持这件事。

00:53:10.989 --> 00:53:11.989
That's right.
这是正确的。

00:53:11.989 --> 00:53:16.869
and embraced that once he was president, which was actually strategically brilliant.
并在他担任总统后接受了这一点，这实际上在战略上是辉煌的。

00:53:16.869 --> 00:53:22.250
But you know, a lot of times culture shifts before politics shifts.
但你知道，很多时候文化先于政治发生转变。

00:53:22.250 --> 00:53:23.150
And it's true.
这是真的。

00:53:23.150 --> 00:53:38.550
You know, they say that like the effect, they called it, I think they called it the Will and Grace effect, that Will and Grace was like an incredibly humanizing, it brought like delightful, it made it no big deal.
你知道，他们说就像这种效果一样，他们称之为“威尔和格蕾丝效应”，威尔和格蕾丝就像一种令人难以置信的人性化，它带来了令人愉快的感觉，这没什么大不了的。

00:53:38.550 --> 00:53:40.510
You know, it made- So comedy can do that.
你知道，它使得-所以喜剧可以做到这一点。

00:53:40.510 --> 00:53:41.550
That's what this episode was.
这就是这一集的内容。

00:53:41.550 --> 00:53:42.389
Comedy can do that.
喜剧可以做到这一点。

00:53:42.389 --> 00:53:44.309
Comedy can humanize issues.
喜剧可以使问题变得人性化。

00:53:44.309 --> 00:53:46.989
And I think that's what we wanted to do without being preachy about it.
我认为这就是我们想要做的，但又不想说教。

00:53:46.989 --> 00:53:48.269
We wanted it to be funny.
我们希望它变得有趣。

00:53:48.269 --> 00:53:53.630
But if you look underneath the funny and we're saying something, but how everybody's equal, everybody should be able to love whoever they want.
但如果你仔细看看有趣的事情，我们会说，每个人都是平等的，每个人都应该能够爱他们想要的任何人。

00:53:53.630 --> 00:53:59.150
And that Barney should be able to hit marriage as an institution and having nothing to do with the people that are getting married.
巴尼应该能够将婚姻视为一种制度，与结婚的人无关。

00:53:59.150 --> 00:54:03.090
And it's true, thinking back 19 years, things were very different.
确实，回想 19 年前，情况已经大不相同。

00:54:03.090 --> 00:54:10.789
By the way, Neil Patrick Harris in season two, that's the moment he publicly announced that he was a gay man and he was a gay man.
顺便说一句，尼尔·帕特里克·哈里斯在第二季中，就在那时他公开宣布自己是同性恋，而且他是同性恋。

00:54:10.789 --> 00:54:15.750
I don't remember, it was kind of right around when this episode was being shot and came out, I think.
我不记得了，我想大概是在这一集拍摄和上映的时候。

00:54:15.750 --> 00:54:27.429
We'll maybe hopefully someday get to talk to Neil about that, but it was really interesting to us that there we were in this moment where Neil was saying, hey, this is who I am, I'm playing this womanizing guy, but I'm a gay man.
也许有一天我们会和尼尔讨论这个问题，但对我们来说真的很有趣的是，尼尔在这一刻说，嘿，这就是我，我正在扮演这个好色之徒，但我是一个同性恋。

00:54:27.429 --> 00:54:35.429
I have a very serious partner who then went on to marry, and it was just interesting to explore all of that 19 years ago in 2006, right?
我有一个非常认真的伴侣，后来他结婚了，19 年前的 2006 年探索这一切很有趣，对吧？

00:54:35.429 --> 00:54:37.750
And that's part of what led to this episode.
这就是导致这一集的部分原因。

00:54:37.750 --> 00:54:48.780
Did you guys think of it as, I don't think you guys thought of this as social activism of any kind, because that would make it less funny in certain ways.
你们是否认为这是，我不认为你们认为这是任何形式的社会活动，因为这会在某些方面使它变得不那么有趣。

00:54:48.780 --> 00:54:58.019
I don't think you had an ideological agenda, but by making it no big deal, it became incredibly political.
我不认为你有意识形态议程，但通过让它不是什么大不了的事情，它变得令人难以置信的政治性。

00:54:58.019 --> 00:54:59.019
Yes.
是的。

00:54:59.019 --> 00:55:10.099
If you point out the absurdity of making it a big deal at all, and Barney's attitude just against marriage in general, so absurd, that we had fun with it before we were trying to preach about it.
如果你指出把它当作一件大事的荒谬之处，以及巴尼反对婚姻的态度，那么荒谬，以至于我们在试图宣扬它之前就已经玩得很开心了。

00:55:10.099 --> 00:55:14.139
We were trying to just have fun with it, and if you look underneath, there's something actually being said there.
我们只是想从中获得乐趣，如果你往下看，就会发现里面确实有东西在说。

00:55:14.139 --> 00:55:30.099
The fact that you guys were nominated for a GLAD Media Award really speaks to the effectiveness, like something of in this particular moment, in this particular time with those particular politics, like just putting something on the air that was like a shrug around the whole thing.
你们获得 GLAD 媒体奖提名这一事实确实说明了有效性，就像在这个特定的时刻、在这个特定的政治时期，就像只是在广播中播放一些对整个事件耸耸肩的东西。

00:55:30.099 --> 00:55:34.500
was I think like really smart and really effective, you know.
我认为非常聪明而且非常有效，你知道。

00:55:34.500 --> 00:55:39.619
Barney Stinson's all-time idol in the entire universe is gay.
巴尼·斯廷森在整个宇宙中的偶像是同性恋。

00:55:39.619 --> 00:55:40.659
Right.
正确的。

00:55:40.659 --> 00:55:43.619
Is a gay man who has a better game than Barney.
是一个比巴尼玩得更好的同性恋者。

00:55:44.260 --> 00:55:49.059
And Barney learned everything he knows from this gay, his gay, black older brother.
巴尼从这个同性恋、他的同性恋黑人哥哥那里学到了他所知道的一切。

00:55:49.059 --> 00:55:52.500
And we thought, no other shows doing exactly this storyline.
我们认为，没有其他节目能完全讲述这个故事情节。

00:55:52.500 --> 00:55:57.059
That's when you're a little excited, you're a little scared, you're a little like, what the hell are we doing here?
那时你会有点兴奋，有点害怕，你会想，我们到底在这里做什么？

00:55:57.059 --> 00:55:59.940
But those are the things that chase and we were excited to do.
但这些都是我们所追求的、我们很高兴做的事情。

00:55:59.940 --> 00:56:08.340
I do remember Craig, sometimes I would ask you or Carter for like, you know, I was always like, how much do I want to know what's coming?
我确实记得克雷格，有时我会问你或卡特，你知道，我总是想，我有多想知道即将发生的事情？

00:56:08.340 --> 00:56:10.820
But I would often say like, what's coming down the pike?
但我经常会问，接下来会发生什么？

00:56:10.820 --> 00:56:12.059
Like, what do you guys got?
比如，你们有什么？

00:56:12.059 --> 00:56:21.739
And you, I remember you saying like, we're writing an episode about Barney's brother and he's gay and he's black, but otherwise completely like Barney in every other way.
而你，我记得你说过，我们正在写一集关于巴尼的兄弟的故事，他是同性恋，他是黑人，但在其他方面完全像巴尼。

00:56:21.739 --> 00:56:25.380
Yeah, I just thought that was such a funny idea.
是的，我只是觉得这是一个很有趣的想法。

00:56:25.380 --> 00:56:27.300
Yeah, that was it, that was the spark.
是的，就是这样，这就是火花。

00:56:27.300 --> 00:56:29.460
We hit that and we said, that's gold.
我们击中了它，我们说，那是黄金。

00:56:29.460 --> 00:56:34.099
and then we said we have to cast it with the perfect person and I like to believe that we shared it.
然后我们说我们必须与完美的人一起选角，我愿意相信我们分享了它。

00:56:34.099 --> 00:56:36.059
And Wayne, thank you for doing this.
韦恩，谢谢你所做的一切。

00:56:36.059 --> 00:56:37.340
Yeah, thanks so much, Wayne.
是的，非常感谢，韦恩。

00:56:37.340 --> 00:56:39.179
And yeah, we'll see you next time.
是的，我们下次见。

00:56:39.179 --> 00:56:40.300
Thanks.
谢谢。

00:56:40.300 --> 00:56:42.710
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:56:42.710 --> 00:56:44.590
Please equip me.
请装备我。

00:56:44.590 --> 00:56:46.909
All sins are forgiven.
所有的罪孽都被宽恕了。

00:56:46.909 --> 00:56:49.110
In New York City.
在纽约市。

